zerosdr (0.3.9) trixie; urgency=medium

  * ADSB radar: map background with Esri / AMap / OSM providers (dark by
    default for AMap and OSM), proxy support, cached patches and a RADAR
    shortcut in the page menu
  * ADSB radar: R/T zoom, gyro heading-up compass, translucent panels and
    automatic recovery when readsb stops updating aircraft.json
  * ADSB detail: full-height PFD with a larger attitude ball / rounded
    square option (M), pitch ladder, bank pointer, scrolling speed and
    altitude tapes, independent altitude wheels and an audio variometer
  * ADSB list: nearest-first order and long-press F to jump to the top
  * ADSB settings: map source in the L menu and in the H overlay
  * First-run guide: mention M for the SDR / radar colour theme

 -- Weiming Feng <bestedwin@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:56:00 +0800

zerosdr (0.3.8) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Tab now opens a translucent page menu (SDR / Spectrum / ADSB) instead of
    switching pages immediately
  * Wideband spectrum page: always uses the tuner AGC (manual gain amplified
    the RTL-SDR's 28.8 MHz clock spur), Space toggles display smoothing
    (median over about 1 MHz, mixed 50/50 with the raw trace), and max hold
    now decays at 1.5 dB/s instead of holding forever
  * ADSB radar can be heading-up: the rose, blips and sweep follow the
    BMI270 + BMM150 compass; I toggles heading-up and 0 stores a zero offset
  * ADSB position editor: L opens it from the list view too, southern and
    western coordinates work (the symbol layer reports its minus as KEY_KP7),
    the first-run guide accepts a minus and rejects incomplete values, and a
    saved position returns to the view it was opened from
  * Q no longer quits immediately; the two second Esc hold is the only exit

 -- Weiming Feng <bestedwin@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:30:00 +0800

zerosdr (0.3.7) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New wideband spectrum page (Tab now cycles SDR -> Spectrum -> ADSB):
    a qspectrumanalyzer style sweep over a user supplied start/stop range,
    1.024 MHz slices stitched into one trace with a waterfall below, a 3/5
    spectrum and 2/5 waterfall split, a smoothed trace, pan/zoom, max hold
    (on by default) and a translucent help overlay; the range is saved in
    the spectrum section of the config file and the capture is released
    when the page is left
  * All settings move into one JSON file, ~/.config/zerosdr/config.json
    (system / sdr / spectrum / adsb); the old sdr_settings.json,
    spectrum_range.txt, adsb_config.json and guide.json are imported once
  * Fn+D / Fn+S adjust the system sink volume on every page, including the
    help overlays and the range/position editors; the SDR status bar
    follows the sink and the spectrum/ADSB pages show a VOL popup
  * M now cycles spectrum and waterfall colour themes (DEFAULT, CLASSIC,
    TURBO, INFERNO, VIRIDIS, PLASMA); DEFAULT keeps the original
    green/blue look
  * Esc only quits after a two second hold, with a rounded progress prompt,
    and now also leaves the radar and detail views
  * Coarse tuning moved to Alt+Left/Right (Alt+Z/C on the keypad)
  * Screenshots (Fn+P) are written to the home directory
  * The SDR status bar shows the demodulation mode in red
  * Help overlay: the key list and the settings tab are grouped and the
    settings hint is highlighted; the ADSB and spectrum pages draw theirs
    as a translucent rounded popup
  * Radar: the scope fills the screen height, the list shows the distance
    unit, non-selected rows are brighter and the counter is labelled
    Traffic
  * Removed the Page Up/Down shortcuts, which collided with the volume keys
  * CI: build with the current action versions and install FreeType

 -- Weiming Feng <bestedwin@gmail.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:40:00 +0800

zerosdr (0.3.6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * ADSB: no position is ever invented. The legacy settings menu shows
    NOT SET instead of 0.0 when nothing is configured, a config file only
    counts as a position when both coordinates parse and are in range, and
    the 0/0 pair written by CLEAR POSITION stays unset after a restart
  * ADSB: saving a manual position validates the typed values instead of
    calling std::stod on unchecked input
  * The configuration path follows $HOME instead of /home/pi

 -- Weiming Feng <bestedwin@gmail.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:20:00 +0800

zerosdr (0.3.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * H -> settings -> SHOW GUIDE now opens the guide immediately instead of
    only arming it for the next start; the ADSB page reloads the observer
    position when entering, so changes made in the guide apply at once
  * Audio: fall back to pulse / pipewire / plughw when ALSA "default" is
    unavailable (store images may not ship the ALSA-to-PipeWire bridge),
    and depend on libasound2-plugins so the pulse route exists

